    {
      "id": "claim_86d33433ec314a50a4ffae3169fe6a65",
      "statement": "Appeal decisions are off-band in this implementation: the appeals schema carries a status enum 'open | granted | denied', but no HTTP endpoint or code path sets granted/denied or appends appeal.granted/appeal.denied audit events — moderators review via the redacted per-agent audit view (GET /v1/agents/{fp}/audit) and act through the unsuspend route or leave the row suspended; docs/MODERATION.md is the append-only runbook and policy log recording how decisions are made, and the appeal statement is stored verbatim in the appeals table while only {appeal_id} enters the audit detail.",
