    {
      "id": "claim_3980e795b6de41a8a71f675beb605c66",
      "statement": "Divergence from docs/MODERATION.md and SPEC: suspended agents cannot heartbeat in the implemented code — store.heartbeat requires row status 'listed' and heartbeat_v1 gates on is_live_row, so a suspended agent's heartbeat fails with UNKNOWN_OR_EXPIRED and its TTL is not extended during suspension (a suspended row whose TTL elapses simply stays suspended because prune_expired only transitions 'listed' rows); the runbook claim that heartbeats stay accepted during appeal review describes intent, not this implementation.",
